Here is a complete, production-ready web application built with **Node.js**, **Express**, and **SQLite** (using `better-sqlite3`).

SQLite natively handles concurrency via file locking, and by wrapping the capacity check and insertion inside a single `IMMEDIATE` transaction, it guarantees that race conditions cannot overbook seats.

---

### Project Setup

1. Create a project directory and initialize it:
   ```bash
   mkdir workshop-signup
   cd workshop-signup
   npm init -y
   ```

2. Install dependencies:
   ```bash
   npm install express better-sqlite3
   ```

3. Ensure your `package.json` has `"type": "module"`:
   ```json
   {
     "type": "module"
   }
   ```

---

### 1. Backend Server (`server.js`)

```javascript
import express from 'express';
import Database from 'better-sqlite3';
import path from 'path';
import { fileURLToPath } from 'url';

const __filename = fileURLToPath(import.meta.url);
const __dirname = path.dirname(__filename);

const app = express();
const PORT = 3000;
const MAX_SEATS = 20;

// Setup SQLite database
const db = new Database('workshop.db');

// WAL mode improves concurrency handling
db.pragma('journal_mode = WAL');

// Initialize schema
db.exec(`
  CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS registrations (
    id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,
    name TEXT NOT NULL,
    email TEXT UNIQUE NOT NULL COLLATE NOCASE,
    created_at DATETIME DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
  );
`);

app.use(express.json());
app.use(express.static(path.join(__dirname, 'public')));

// Prepared statements
const countQuery = db.prepare('SELECT COUNT(*) AS count FROM registrations');
const insertQuery = db.prepare('INSERT INTO registrations (name, email) VALUES (?, ?)');

// ATOMIC REGISTRATION TRANSACTION
// db.transaction() in better-sqlite3 automatically executes a BEGIN IMMEDIATE
// which acquires a write lock, preventing race conditions from simultaneous requests.
const registerParticipant = db.transaction((name, email) => {
  const { count } = countQuery.get();

  if (count >= MAX_SEATS) {
    const error = new Error('Workshop is fully booked.');
    error.code = 'FULL';
    throw error;
  }

  insertQuery.run(name, email);
  return { seatsRemaining: MAX_SEATS - (count + 1) };
});

// GET: Seat status (Zero PII exposed)
app.get('/api/status', (req, res) => {
  try {
    const { count } = countQuery.get();
    res.json({
      totalSeats: MAX_SEATS,
      bookedSeats: count,
      seatsRemaining: Math.max(0, MAX_SEATS - count),
      isFull: count >= MAX_SEATS
    });
  } catch (err) {
    res.status(500).json({ error: 'Failed to retrieve status.' });
  }
});

// POST: Register a participant
app.post('/api/register', (req, res) => {
  const { name, email } = req.body;

  // Basic validation
  if (!name || !email || typeof name !== 'string' || typeof email !== 'string') {
    return res.status(400).json({ error: 'Valid name and email are required.' });
  }

  const cleanName = name.trim();
  const cleanEmail = email.trim().toLowerCase();

  const emailRegex = /^[^\s@]+@[^\s@]+\.[^\s@]+$/;
  if (!emailRegex.test(cleanEmail)) {
    return res.status(400).json({ error: 'Invalid email address.' });
  }

  try {
    const result = registerParticipant(cleanName, cleanEmail);
    res.status(201).json({
      message: 'Registration successful! Your seat is reserved.',
      seatsRemaining: result.seatsRemaining
    });
  } catch (err) {
    if (err.code === 'SQLITE_CONSTRAINT_UNIQUE') {
      return res.status(409).json({ error: 'This email address is already registered.' });
    }
    if (err.code === 'FULL') {
      return res.status(410).json({ error: 'Sorry, the workshop is already full.' });
    }
    console.error(err);
    res.status(500).json({ error: 'Internal server error.' });
  }
});

app.listen(PORT, () => {
  console.log(`Server running at http://localhost:${PORT}`);
});
```

---

### 2. Frontend Interface (`public/index.html`)

Create a folder named `public` and add `index.html`:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Workshop Sign-up</title>
  <style>
    :root {
      --primary: #2563eb;
      --success: #16a34a;
      --danger: #dc2626;
      --gray: #6b7280;
    }
    body {
      font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
      background: #f3f4f6;
      display: grid;
      place-items: center;
      min-height: 100vh;
      margin: 0;
    }
    .card {
      background: white;
      padding: 2rem;
      border-radius: 8px;
      box-shadow: 0 4px 6px -1px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.1);
      width: 100%;
      max-width: 400px;
    }
    h1 { margin-top: 0; font-size: 1.5rem; text-align: center; }
    .badge {
      display: block;
      text-align: center;
      padding: 0.5rem;
      background: #e0f2fe;
      color: #0369a1;
      border-radius: 4px;
      margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
      font-weight: 500;
    }
    .form-group { margin-bottom: 1rem; }
    label { display: block; margin-bottom: 0.25rem; font-size: 0.875rem; }
    input {
      width: 100%;
      padding: 0.5rem;
      border: 1px solid #d1d5db;
      border-radius: 4px;
      box-sizing: border-box;
    }
    button {
      width: 100%;
      padding: 0.75rem;
      background: var(--primary);
      color: white;
      border: none;
      border-radius: 4px;
      cursor: pointer;
      font-size: 1rem;
    }
    button:disabled { background: var(--gray); cursor: not-allowed; }
    .message {
      margin-top: 1rem;
      padding: 0.75rem;
      border-radius: 4px;
      display: none;
      font-size: 0.875rem;
    }
    .message.error { background: #fee2e2; color: var(--danger); display: block; }
    .message.success { background: #dcfce7; color: var(--success); display: block; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

  <div class="card">
    <h1>Workshop Sign-up</h1>
    <div id="seatCounter" class="badge">Loading seat availability...</div>

    <form id="signupForm">
      <div class="form-group">
        <label for="name">Full Name</label>
        <input type="text" id="name" required autocomplete="name" />
      </div>

      <div class="form-group">
        <label for="email">Email Address</label>
        <input type="email" id="email" required autocomplete="email" />
      </div>

      <button type="submit" id="submitBtn">Reserve Seat</button>
    </form>

    <div id="message" class="message"></div>
  </div>

  <script>
    const form = document.getElementById('signupForm');
    const submitBtn = document.getElementById('submitBtn');
    const messageEl = document.getElementById('message');
    const counterEl = document.getElementById('seatCounter');

    async function updateAvailability() {
      try {
        const res = await fetch('/api/status');
        const data = await res.json();

        if (data.isFull) {
          counterEl.textContent = 'Workshop is Full (0 seats remaining)';
          counterEl.style.background = '#fee2e2';
          counterEl.style.color = '#dc2626';
          submitBtn.disabled = true;
          submitBtn.textContent = 'Sold Out';
        } else {
          counterEl.textContent = `${data.seatsRemaining} of ${data.totalSeats} seats remaining`;
          counterEl.style.background = '#e0f2fe';
          counterEl.style.color = '#0369a1';
          submitBtn.disabled = false;
        }
      } catch (err) {
        counterEl.textContent = 'Could not load seat count';
      }
    }

    form.addEventListener('submit', async (e) => {
      e.preventDefault();
      messageEl.className = 'message';
      messageEl.style.display = 'none';
      submitBtn.disabled = true;

      const payload = {
        name: document.getElementById('name').value,
        email: document.getElementById('email').value
      };

      try {
        const res = await fetch('/api/register', {
          method: 'POST',
          headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
          body: JSON.stringify(payload)
        });

        const data = await res.json();

        if (!res.ok) {
          throw new Error(data.error || 'Something went wrong.');
        }

        messageEl.textContent = data.message;
        messageEl.className = 'message success';
        form.reset();
      } catch (err) {
        messageEl.textContent = err.message;
        messageEl.className = 'message error';
      } finally {
        await updateAvailability();
      }
    });

    updateAvailability();
  </script>
</body>
</html>
```

---

### How the Requirements Are Met:

1. **Email Uniqueness:** The table defines `email TEXT UNIQUE NOT NULL COLLATE NOCASE`. Any attempt to register an already-present email will fail at the database level and return an HTTP `409 Conflict`.
2. **Atomic Seat Limit Protection:** The function `registerParticipant` is a prepared transaction. SQLite locks the file during `db.transaction(...)`, meaning even under heavy concurrent load, the read (`SELECT COUNT(*)`) and write (`INSERT`) happen in isolation. If count is $\ge 20$, the transaction rolls back, preventing overbooking.
3. **Data Privacy (Zero PII Exposed):** The only public endpoint returning list info is `/api/status`, which only outputs aggregated numbers (`totalSeats`, `bookedSeats`, `seatsRemaining`). The list of names and emails is never accessible via any API route.

### Run the App
```bash
node server.js
```
Open `http://localhost:3000` in your browser.

